     "metadata": {}
    },
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "  CLIP hidden size: 768\n",
      "  Gemma hidden size: 640\n",
      "  CLIP frozen. It is a teacher/scaffold only; final inference uses the pruned Gemma-only checkpoint.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# @title 2.2 Load CLIP Persistently (training scaffold / teacher)\n",
    "from transformers import CLIPTextModel, CLIPTokenizer\n",
    "\n",
    "CLIP_ID = \"openai/clip-vit-large-patch14\"\n",
    "print(f\"Loading CLIP scaffold: {CLIP_ID}\")\n",
    "clip_tokenizer = CLIPTokenizer.from_pretrained(CLIP_ID)\n",
    "clip_model = CLIPTextModel.from_pretrained(\n",
    "    CLIP_ID,\n",
    "    torch_dtype=torch.float16,\n",
    ").to(device).eval()\n",
    "for p in clip_model.parameters():\n",
    "    p.requires_grad = False\n",
    "\n",
    "clip_hidden_size = clip_model.config.hidden_size  # 768 for ViT-L/14\n",
    "print(f\"  CLIP hidden size: {clip_hidden_size}\")\n",
    "print(f\"  Gemma hidden size: {gemma_hidden_size}\")\n",
    "assert clip_hidden_size == 768, \"SD1.5 UNet expects CLIP hidden size 768\"\n",
    "assert gemma_hidden_size == 640, \"Gemma 3 270M expected hidden size 640\"\n",
    "print(\"  CLIP frozen. It is a teacher/scaffold only; final inference uses the pruned Gemma-only checkpoint.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "TN_b_f69A76y"
   },
   "source": [
    "## Legacy linear bake removed\n",
    "\n",
    "The previous static ridge/bake route is intentionally removed from the mainline. Runtime evidence showed the linear map collapsed to near-zero signal, so this notebook now learns native Gemma attention behavior through the UNet instead.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "IXJjeEK3A76y"
   },
   "source": [
    "## No static embedding target\n",
    "\n",
    "We do not train Gemma to imitate CLIP embeddings. Gemma remains frozen and supplies hidden states; the UNet learns a native Gemma-conditioning branch under a frozen CLIP teacher/scaffold.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "_WD7AXGWLE1K"
   },
   "source": [
    "## Section 3: Dual Cross-Attention UNet Setup\n",
    "\n",
    "Every SD1.5 cross-attention block keeps its original CLIP `attn2` path and gains a parallel Gemma-native attention path. `clip_scale` and `gemma_scale` control the transition.\n"
   ]
  },
